# Spark DS — Token Hierarchy

Spark uses three tiers: **Primitive → Semantic → Component**.

## Rules

| Tier | Prefix | Use in React/CSS |
|------|--------|------------------|
| Primitive | `--primitive-*` | **Never** for colors in app UI. Spacing scale (`--primitive-space-*`) is OK per `dimensions.html`. |
| Semantic | `--semantic-*` | Default for layout, text, surfaces, borders, motion. |
| Component | `--semantic-button-*`, etc. | When a component token exists for that element. |

## Styling in React

```tsx
// Bad — hardcoded values
<div style={{ color: '#008EF5', padding: 12 }} />

// Bad — primitive in component CSS
.button { background: var(--primitive-blue-500); }

// Good — semantic or component tokens
.button {
  color: var(--semantic-content-brand);
  padding: var(--semantic-button-padding-x-medium);
  background: var(--semantic-button-primary-bg-default);
}
```

## Token groups

- **Content:** `--semantic-content-*`
- **Surface:** `--semantic-surface-*`
- **Border:** `--semantic-border-*`
- **Typography:** `--semantic-typography-*`
- **Shadow / focus:** `--semantic-shadow-*`
- **Motion:** `--semantic-motion-*`

Import `tokens.css` at the app root. Reference tokens via `var()` in CSS Modules, global CSS, or styled wrappers. Avoid inline styles except for dynamic layout that has no token.
